---
import MainLayout from "../../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import ContactSection from "../../../../components/ContactSection.astro";
import LanguageSupportBanner from "../../../../components/LanguageSupportBanner.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../../../../data/site";
import { withBase } from "../../../../utils/withBase";
import { getServicePath, getServices } from "../../../../data/services";

const businessServices = await getServices("business", "en");
---

<MainLayout
  title={`IT Support Berlin | Business IT Services | ${siteConfig.defaultTitleSuffix}`}
  description="English-speaking IT support in Berlin for small and growing businesses: networks, Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, workplace IT, backup and practical IT projects."
  canonicalPath="en/services/business/"
  lang="en"
  alternatePath="leistungen/unternehmen/"
>
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Business IT services</span>
      <h1 class="section-title">IT Support for Businesses in Berlin</h1>
      <p class="section-lead">
        We help small and growing businesses, offices, practices, studios, shops and independent
        professionals across Berlin with concrete IT problems, planned changes and reliable
        workplace infrastructure. A long-term support contract is not required to work with us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <LanguageSupportBanner locale="en" />

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Common situations</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">When your IT needs to grow with the business — or simply work reliably again</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        You do not need to arrive with a technical diagnosis. Many requests start with a new office,
        a recurring disruption, a cloud-service problem or a workplace setup that has become harder
        to manage as the business has grown.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>New workplaces or office changes</h3>
          <p>
            Computers, users, email, printers, shared storage and the network need to work together
            from the start rather than becoming separate fixes later.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Problems affecting day-to-day work</h3>
          <p>
            Windows or software faults, unreliable connections, access problems and recurring
            interruptions are assessed by their operational impact and likely cause.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Cloud, email and collaboration</h3>
          <p>
            Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace should fit the people, devices, permissions and
            working practices of the organisation rather than creating more friction.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Devices, data and backup</h3>
          <p>
            New computers, shared storage, NAS, backup and existing peripherals can be planned as
            part of one practical workplace environment.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Specialist areas</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Three business IT services with their own detailed pages</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        For larger or clearly defined projects, these pages go deeper into planning, implementation
        and typical project questions. This landing page remains the broad starting point when your
        request crosses more than one area.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        {businessServices.map((service) => (
          <a class="card service-card-link" href={withBase(getServicePath(service))}>
            <h3>{service.hero.title}</h3>
            <p>{service.seo.description}</p>
            <span class="service-link-label">View service →</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container two-grid">
      <section>
        <span class="eyebrow">Planned IT projects</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Build, modernise and extend your workplace IT deliberately</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          A new office, additional staff or ageing infrastructure can be a good moment to improve the
          underlying setup instead of adding another isolated workaround.
        </p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Set up new or additional workstations and devices</li>
          <li>Plan office networks, Wi-Fi, cabling, NAS and secure remote access</li>
          <li>Set up or improve Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace environments</li>
          <li>Recommend suitable hardware and arrange procurement when agreed</li>
          <li>Include backup, shared storage and important access requirements in the project</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <span class="eyebrow">Problems & support</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Practical help when existing systems interrupt the workday</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          A single fault can still have a serious business impact. We first establish what is not
          working, who is affected and what depends on it before making changes.
        </p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Investigate Windows workstations, software, printers and peripherals</li>
          <li>Trace email, account, synchronisation and access problems</li>
          <li>Investigate office network and Wi-Fi issues methodically</li>
          <li>Distinguish a recurring underlying problem from a one-off symptom</li>
          <li>Recommend follow-up work or modernisation only where it is useful</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Ways to work with us</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">IT support without a mandatory managed-service contract</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        Planning, installation, migration, modernisation and specific troubleshooting can all be
        standalone engagements. If recurring maintenance or support makes sense later, it can be
        discussed separately.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>One-off projects</h3>
          <p>A defined project can be planned, implemented, tested and handed over as a complete piece of work.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Targeted troubleshooting</h3>
          <p>You can also contact us for a specific fault or a clearly bounded technical requirement.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Optional ongoing support</h3>
          <p>Recurring maintenance or support is agreed only when it suits the business and the actual need.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">How we work</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">From the business need to a clear technical outcome</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        The technical depth depends on the project, but the process stays understandable: establish
        the need, agree the scope, carry out the work and check the result.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>1. Understand the need</h3>
          <p>We clarify what is failing or what needs to be built and which people or workflows are affected.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>2. Define the scope</h3>
          <p>Existing systems, dependencies, required access and the intended outcome are reviewed before changes begin.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>3. Implement</h3>
          <p>The agreed work is carried out on site in Berlin or with suitable remote support where that is practical.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>4. Test & hand over</h3>
          <p>Important functions are checked and relevant changes or next steps are explained clearly at handover.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container two-grid">
      <section>
        <span class="eyebrow">Technical breadth</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Business IT is more than individual computers</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          A working desk often depends on the network, user accounts, data, cloud services and shared
          resources behind it. Those relationships can be handled as part of the same project without
          turning the public page into a catalogue of protocols and products.
        </p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Windows workstations, printers and peripherals</li>
          <li>Microsoft 365 and Google Workspace</li>
          <li>Office networks, business Wi-Fi and structured cabling</li>
          <li>NAS, shared storage, backup and cloud storage</li>
          <li>VPN, email, domains, users and access structures</li>
          <li>Windows Server/Active Directory and Linux server work assessed as separate project areas</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <aside class="feature-rail">
        <span class="eyebrow">Experience</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0.45rem;">IT experience since 2008</h3>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.6rem; color: var(--ink-700);">
          The aim is not to list every technology we have encountered. It is to understand the
          existing environment responsibly and define a scope that fits the real system and business
          impact.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="container two-grid">
      <section>
        <span class="eyebrow">Access & changes</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Clear agreement before changes to important systems</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">
          Before changing accounts, email, shared data or production devices, we clarify the access
          required and the intended result. Where a change carries meaningful risk, backup or a
          suitable fallback should be part of the plan.
        </p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Access only as far as necessary for the agreed work</li>
          <li>Explain consequential changes and expected impact before proceeding</li>
          <li>Plan backups or other safeguards where they are technically appropriate</li>
          <li>No invented security, compliance, availability or response-time guarantees</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <aside class="feature-rail">
        <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">On-site IT support across Berlin</h3>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.4rem; color: var(--ink-700);">
          We accept enquiries from small and growing businesses across Berlin. Fit is assessed by the
          project, complexity, operational risk and a responsible way to deliver the work — not by a
          published employee or device threshold.
        </p>
        <div class="district-list">
          {siteConfig.serviceDistricts.map((district) => <span class="district-pill">{district}</span>)}
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">What businesses often want to know before getting in touch</h2>
      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Do we need to sign a long-term IT support contract?</h3>
          <p>No. One-off projects, upgrades and specific troubleshooting can be commissioned independently. Recurring support is optional.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Do you work with small businesses that do not have an internal IT team?</h3>
          <p>Yes. The important questions are the task, technical environment and whether the work can be delivered responsibly. We do not publish a rigid minimum or maximum company size.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Can you set up a new office or new workstations?</h3>
          <p>Yes. Depending on the project, network, devices, users, cloud services, shared storage, printers and backup can be planned and set up together.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Can you recommend or supply hardware?</h3>
          <p>Yes. Where it is part of the project, we can recommend suitable computers and network equipment and arrange procurement within the agreed scope.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Can the technical work and explanations be handled in English?</h3>
          <p>Yes. English-speaking technical service is available, including on-site work in Berlin where the project requires it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Do you take on Windows Server or Linux projects?</h3>
          <p>These projects can be assessed according to the environment and scope. Larger Windows Server/Active Directory and Linux server work is treated as its own technical project area.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Can you quote a fixed price immediately?</h3>
          <p>If the scope is sufficiently clear, we can discuss an expected scope or quotation in advance. When the cause is uncertain, a paid diagnostic visit may be required first.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSection locale="en" context="business" />
</MainLayout>
